Z||000019||Nashco||08-23-2001||02:19 AM||||Partially finished projects...school delaying things...gremlins I'm working away at...money pit always needing more...bah<P>That's what I say..bah...that's what I love about my fiero!  I'm constantly fixing, upgrading, tuning, tweaking, talking up, putting down, playing with, and abusing my fiero.  You know why?  Because I can...I don't want some economy car that everybody has and nobody does anything with them.  I don't want something that runs like a top and I haven't had to touch it for 8 years.  I want character; that's why I also own an old VW bug...the same reasons.  Yeah, once you go through EVERYTHING the car runs great and drives great, but by the time you're done going through it all, you have more ideas.  That's the beauty of it all, it's never done, it's in constant progression towards being better.  Cheer up folks, once you find that gremlin, you'll be more educated and VERY pleased with what you got done.  Oh, and once you've replaced a part, you know it's good for another 10 years, so that's an added benefit!<P>Smile, it's all good <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
