Z||000040||Jncomutt||08-24-2001||02:56 AM||||My turn to vent.  Just when you have some money saved up to put in the car, you decide to buy something added or something to upgrade or tweak.  And then the next damn week ya gotta do major work.  ie. clutch, rear main seal, finding out why the heck the damn AC Compressor won't go on after all obvious reasons eliminated, new axle shaft/CV joint.  And you wish you hadn't spent the money the week b4 because now you need the money for repairs.  Grrr.... Damn car was running great.  Had $1100 saved in my "fiero fund"  Buy a pair of rims and tires.  Put em on the car.  Clutch was slipping.  Needed to drive the car to work so I can get money for the "Fiero Fund"  Over the week of driving the car I think I've totally killed it.  Damn thing shakes and slams, and I need a new flywheel now, and tranny mounts, and engine mount, and still need to get everything in the damn car somehow, and starting first year of college, and GRRRR!!!||||reg||1
Z||000041||Fiero*101||08-24-2001||08:45 AM||||ok ive been pissed for 2 months now<BR>im a senior in High School and i just bought my 86 Fiero SE 2M6 in June. And i bought it knowing that it needed work and it did and i worked on it all summer im now in my 4th day of school. and this is what i fixed so far. <BR>1.well when i bought it the taillights didnt work.(DAMN GROUND WIRE!!!)(15 hours)hahaha<BR>2.my Interior was a MESS these are SWEEEEET CARS i dont know how in the HELL any body could treat it like that. ASHES evry where stains on my carpets and seat is torn to $h**<BR>(about 6 hours to Clean it)<BR>3. Had to change all the fuses<BR>4. then the Alternator went bad!!!<BR>5. DIDNT KNOW HOW TO GET IT OUT TILL MY CHILLTON BOOK CAME.3 WEEKS later!!!!<BR>6.got it out by my dad taking a Bar and beating it out!<BR>7. He broke the Alt Bracket<BR>8.Had to wait another 2 weeks for another one which racked me $50<BR>9.ok then the battery went to hell!<BR>10. ok when i bought it i knew i loved it b/c i alwas wanted one since i was a little kid. my neighbor had an 86 GT it was SWEEEET. ok any way.<P>11.it has a strectched throttle cable and its REaLly pissing me off(I HAVE NO CLUE HOW TO FIX IT YET any IDEAS?)<BR>12. NEEDS new Exahust!!!<BR>13. and the back fram is REALLY rusted but not so bad that its going to fall apart.<BR>14.the battery tray is GONE!!!! i mean its like only half there so my battery is like sitting on half rusted metal and air.<P>and im just waiting to get more money but all my problems i hope will be fixed in the next month.<P>Ok thank you for letting me vent my anger.<P>but im from a little town and for sombody to see a Fiero evry body is like Nice car. and my friend that just got a 92 i think Firebird that looks worst then my car said NICE car what you got in it<BR>and i was like a V6 and i poped the trunk and he was like DAMN!!!! really? i bet you could take me. that little thing must have balls and i was like i dont know it has a streched throtle cable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Well i know it was long but i just thought i would let people w/ problems know there not alone not by any means<P>But I LOVE MY faded Gold 86 2M6<P>Thanks again <BR>Fiero*101||||reg||1
Z||000042||Ryan Wright||08-24-2001||05:05 PM||||OK,<P>I bought a beautiful '85 GT @ ~70k miles and have owned it for 6 years. 2 years ago I put a new 3.1 in it ($2000) and retrofitted the AC to R-134A ($700; replaced damn near *everything*). Two months ago I tore the engine down, pulled the heads, replaced most major seals and scrubbed the hell out of everything. Detailed the engine compartment; painted my dog bone, air cleaner, heat shields, got all of the grease and oil off of everything, etc. You could have eaten off of it.<P>Then, earlier this month, some dirty SOB flew into a road rage, passed me, then tried to clip my front bumper and/or force me to rear-end him. I missed, but nailed a city light post. My '85? Totalled. ( <A HREF="http://www.ryanwright.com/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ryanwright.com/fiero/</A> )<P>I now have a car that more than makes up for the loss of my '85 (info @ the same URL, above), but still... the a$$hole left the scene, came back after the cops arrived, and they STILL let him go! Flat out refused to cite him for anything!! (The good news: My insurance company is suing him. At the very least he's going to have to pay a lawyer some big bucks to defend himself...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Ryan Wright (http://www.ryanwright.com)||||reg||1
Z||000043||fropuff||08-24-2001||05:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ryan Wright:<BR><B>...Then, earlier this month, some dirty SOB flew into a road rage, passed me, then tried to clip my front bumper and/or force me to rear-end him. I missed, but nailed a city light post. My '85? Totalled.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>&gt;Well, I have something similar to be pissed about.  I used to be pissed because it was acting doggy, but now I have a car sitting in the garage with parts hanging down to the floor.  Last night, when pulling out of the gas station parking lot, no one was there.  So I went.  Then I hear a LOUD crunch.  Some faggot was cruisin through the lot at around 35 and totaled the rear end of my '86 GT.  There's around $3000-$5000 damage.  If I don't get insurance money, which I'm sure I frickin won't, I'll have to sell it and take a big-ass loss.  All it did to him was put in a 12" red scrape; easily buffed out.  New van; full coverage.  I hope I get money from the little SOB.  <P>Sorry for the accident though.  Some people don't deserve their frickin licenses.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000044||Joe Torma||08-24-2001||05:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR>[B]  <BR>3.4 = Iron heads.<BR>3400 = Aluminum heads.<BR>What is the TDC? I thought the 3400 was the TDC.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>TWIN DUAL CAM, as far as I know.<BR>The Olds Van is a 3400...you did keep the aluminum heads didn't you?<BR>Get some pics for us!<P>Oh...to comlain, I'm stuck at work.||||reg||1
